Problem Requirements:
1. Find all possible rearrangements of the letters in Stephan's name.
2. Calculate the time needed to write these rearrangements, knowing that Stephan can write twelve rearrangements per minute.
3. Convert the result into hours.

Reasoning Process:
1. Generate all possible permutations of the letters in the name "STEPHAN."
2. Calculate the total number of these permutations.
3. Use the known rate of writing rearrangements to calculate the total time it will take.
4. Convert the time from minutes to hours.

Solution (C# Code):

```csharp
using System;
using System.Linq;

namespace RearrangementProblem
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Total time in hours: {CalculateTotalTime("STEPHAN")} hours");
        }

        static double CalculateTotalTime(string name)
        {
            // Calculate the number of permutations
            int permutations = Factorial(name.Length);

            // Given rate of rearrangements per minute
            double ratePerMinute = 12;

            // Calculate total time in minutes
            double totalMinutes = (double)permutations / ratePerMinute;

            // Convert to hours
            return totalMinutes / 60;
        }

        static int Factorial(int number)
        {
            // Calculate factorial to get the number of permutations
            return number <= 1 ? 1 : number * Factorial(number - 1);
        }
    }
}
```

