Since \( 9901 \) is a prime number, the prime factors of \( 10001 \) are \( 101 \) and \( 9901 \). These factors are the greatest common divisors of the eight-digit integer.

Therefore, the greatest common divisor (GCD) of all eight-digit integers of this form is:
\[
101
